<title>USA: High Plains Wheat - Planting advances quickly.</title>
<headline>High Plains Wheat - Planting advances quickly.</headline>
<dateline>KANSAS CITY, Mo. 1996-10-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Planting of hard red winter wheat in the central Plains was advancing rapidly as the weather remained dry, grain dealers said Friday.</p>
<p>&quot;Everybody's trying to plant wheat. They have plenty of soil moisture and everything,&quot; an Oklahoma merchandiser said. &quot;It's supposed to be dry for the next five days so it'll probably continue to go well.&quot;</p>
<p>But as farmers sought to get as much fieldwork completed as possible, farmer selling of wheat remained slack.</p>
<p>Basis bids were mostly unchanged, although one dealer said basis had firmed slightly at the Gulf.  </p>
